body:
Execute Ticket 3 (t-run2-w3-mcp-plan-gates) for Release Audit Run 2.

IMPORTANT HEADLESS WORKER RULES:
- Use ONLY view_file, replace_file_content, and write_to_file.
- Do NOT call run_command (the scheduler automatically runs the test suite in the gating phase immediately after you finish editing).
- Only edit files in your declared scope.

1. In mcp/server.mjs (BLOCKER #2, SHOULD-FIX #11, BACKLOG #4):
   - Add isAbsolute to the import from 'node:path' at line 4 of mcp/server.mjs.
   - In TOOLS (lines 100-106), update agb_doctor's inputSchema.properties from {} to:
     properties: {
       repo: { type: 'string', description: 'Optional path to target repository' }
     }
   - In handleToolCall for agb_plan (around lines 208-215), do NOT unconditionally call resolve(specCheck.value). Instead:
     targetCwd = resolve(repoCheck.value);
     const rawSpec = specCheck.value;
     const specInTarget = resolve(targetCwd, rawSpec);
     const specInAmbient = resolve(rawSpec);
     let resolvedSpec;
     if (existsSync(specInTarget)) {
       resolvedSpec = specInTarget;
     } else if (existsSync(specInAmbient)) {
       resolvedSpec = specInAmbient;
     } else if (isAbsolute(rawSpec) || rawSpec.includes('/') || rawSpec.includes('\\') || /\.(md|markdown|txt|json)$/i.test(rawSpec)) {
       resolvedSpec = specInTarget;
     } else {
       resolvedSpec = rawSpec;
     }
     cliArgs.push('plan', resolvedSpec, targetCwd);
     if (args.out !== undefined) {
       const outCheck = requireNonFlagString(args, 'out');
       if (!outCheck.ok) { sendError(id, -32602, outCheck.error); return; }
       cliArgs.push('--out', resolve(targetCwd, outCheck.value));
     }

2. In lib/plan.mjs (SHOULD-FIX #2):
   - Note: tierCandidates and TIER_CANDIDATES are already imported on line 29 of lib/plan.mjs. Do NOT add a duplicate import.
   - In applyModelRouterTiers (lines 75-78), only mutate t.tier when assignment?.tier is a known tier in TIER_CANDIDATES and has at least one candidate for t.pool_hint:
     for (const t of plan.tickets ?? []) {
       const assignment = byId.get(t.id);
       if (assignment?.tier && TIER_CANDIDATES[assignment.tier] && tierCandidates(assignment.tier, t.pool_hint).length > 0) {
         t.tier = assignment.tier;
       }
     }

3. In lib/prosecute.mjs (BACKLOG #1):
   - At line 143, change:
     const verdict = blocking ? 'block' : parsed.verdict;
     to:
     const verdict = blocking ? 'block' : 'ship';
     so a model returning verdict: 'block' with only medium/low advisory findings does not produce a block with an empty blockingFindings() array.

4. In lib/adlc-bridge.mjs (BACKLOG #2):
   - At line 200 and line 222 inside writeAdlcTickets, replace:
     if (existsSync(dir) && lstatSync(dir).isSymbolicLink())
     and
     if (existsSync(p) && lstatSync(p).isSymbolicLink())
     with:
     if (lstatSync(dir, { throwIfNoEntry: false })?.isSymbolicLink())
     and
     if (lstatSync(p, { throwIfNoEntry: false })?.isSymbolicLink())
     so dangling symlinks at .adlc or .adlc/tickets are caught and throw "refusing to project tickets through a symlink: <p>".

5. In commands/agb-run.md and commands/agb-doctor.md (SHOULD-FIX #11 & BACKLOG #15):
   - In commands/agb-run.md:6 and commands/agb-run.md:15, remove "[options]" so line 6 is "# /agb-run <plan.json>" and line 15 is "~/.local/bin/agb run <plan.json>".
   - In commands/agb-doctor.md, keep "# /agb-doctor" on line 6 and note in the body text that the agb_doctor MCP tool accepts an optional repo parameter.

6. Add unit tests at the end of test/plan.test.mjs, test/prosecute.test.mjs, and test/adlc-bridge.test.mjs covering the changes above.
